- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests`

**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item-model library store's seam in Domain: the entry, its identity, its errors, its record and its in-memory double, with a contract suite any store runs (001 §I '`ItemModel` — parameterised physics, a library entry'; 001 §C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite create', 'Contract tests'; the S7.1 brief: a proxy record, an in-memory implementation and a SQLite create, the S2 pattern; .spec-md §3.3: built-ins are named through well-known ids). In `ItemModels.fs`, after step 208's forms, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1; the file opens `System` (`Guid`). (1) `ItemModelId of Guid` with `.value`, an item model's frozen GUID. `ItemModelVersionId = { itemModelId : ItemModelId; version : VersionNumber }`, one version of one item model, which an item pins (001 §I 'the ItemModel it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted)'). (2) `ItemModelEntry = { id : ItemModelId; name : EntryName; description : EntryDescription; model : ItemModelForm; protection : EntryProtection }`, shaped like `PolarizerPreset` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerPreset`): its protection derives from its provenance at the file seam (step 210). `ItemModelVersion = { version : VersionNumber; entry : ItemModelEntry }`, one stored version, with `member this.versionId : ItemModelVersionId`. (3) `module ItemModelIds`, shaped like `MaterialLibrary.MaterialIds` (no `[<RequireQualifiedAccess>]`, no `[<Literal>]`, each a typed value written `Guid.Parse "…" |> ItemModelId`), the frozen identities of the eleven built-in item models step 210 ships: `realLinearPolarizerModelId` `940bda4e-db9c-4103-b59c-dab2f3ee5875`; `retarderPlateModelId` `8e9797b7-f0db-443f-b33d-61f9901881cd`; `circularPolarizerModelId` `33486eec-836a-4cbf-ac79-e3f14439ad4b`; `blackBoxMuellerModelId` `852cbb95-e9f8-4963-8098-866303071e67`; `emptySlotModelId` `628b87f6-8e8c-460b-8a91-1815063aa9dd`; `intensityDetectorModelId` `01cfdc64-d07e-4e2b-963e-ea3caa8428e6`; `muellerPolarimeterModelId` `7e74324f-ded2-4607-b9d8-a40d477ac437`; `ellipsometerModelId` `608caa06-1b53-464e-962f-073730270af6`. (4) `ItemModelError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`: `DuplicateItemModelErr` (the store already holds an item model under the id, naming it and its held version), `InvalidItemModelErr` (the store cannot hold the entry: a protection or an id it refuses, naming why) and `ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr` (the store beneath failed, carrying the failure's `describe`). `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form: `the item model is already held: <reason>`, `the item model cannot be stored: <reason>` and `the item-model store is unavailable: <reason>`. (5) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ItemModelProxy = { listItemModels : unit -> Result<ItemModelVersion list, ItemModelError>; resolveItemModelVersion : ItemModelVersionId -> Result<ItemModelVersion option, ItemModelError>; saveItemModel : ItemModelVersion -> Result<unit, ItemModelError> }`, the functional-proxy convention of `ElementId.fs:SourceProxy`. Its doc states the contract: `listItemModels` answers the latest version of every item model, ordered by name and then by id; `resolveItemModelVersion` answers that exact version or `None`; `saveItemModel` stores a new item model at the given version and refuses an id the store already holds with `DuplicateItemModelErr`, changing nothing, because an item model is never edited in this spec and a later version arrives through the import seam (step 95). (6) `static member createInMemory () : ItemModelProxy`, the in-memory double: a closure-local map from `ItemModelId` to its saved version, mutated only inside the closure as in `CatalogueProxy.createInMemory` (step 32). It holds what it is given, built-ins included, because step 210's in-memory import pushes the shipped item models through it. No cache, retry, removal, edit or other field is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs`, `module ItemModelProxyTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. Its entries are test-local `UserManaged` item models under test-local GUIDs: `Lab retarder` (a constant retarder) and `Lab polarizer` (a real LP by diattenuation). `[<AbstractClass>] type ItemModelProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshItemModels : unit -> ItemModelProxy`, a store holding no item model, and three `[<Fact>]` members. `an item model is saved at its version and resolved by exactly that version`: `Lab retarder` saved at version 2 resolves at version 2 to the saved version, and answers `None` at version 1 and under another id. `the store lists the latest version of every item model, by name`: after `Lab retarder` and `Lab polarizer` are saved, `listItemModels` answers `Lab polarizer` then `Lab retarder`. `saving an item model the store already holds is DuplicateItemModelErr and keeps the held version`: a second save under `Lab retarder`'s id, at version 3 and with another name, answers `DuplicateItemModelErr` naming the id; version 2 still resolves to the first, and version 3 answers `None`. `type ItemModelProxyTests () = inherit ItemModelProxyContract ()` is the in-memory store (`freshItemModels` is `ItemModelProxy.createInMemory ()`), with its own fact `every item-model error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it. ItemModelIds MUST additionally declare sourcePresetItemModelId with the frozen GUID 239b0cfb-9938-5f3b-a767-c4252ea671b6. ItemModelIds MUST additionally declare idealPolarizerItemModelId with the frozen GUID d47e5ce3-3e74-5058-848e-3aa54930e377. ItemModelIds MUST additionally declare stackSampleItemModelId with the frozen GUID 4d13ecb1-2006-576f-99e7-e8bc266e8624.

**Acceptance.** After the contract lands, `ItemModels.fs` MUST declare `ItemModelProxy` with exactly the fields `listItemModels`, `resolveItemModelVersion` and `saveItemModel`, its in-memory double, the entry types and the eleven `ItemModelIds`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item model is saved at its version and resolved by exactly that version`, `the store lists the latest version of every item model, by name` and `saving an item model the store already holds is DuplicateItemModelErr and keeps the held version` under `ItemModelProxyTests` and `every item-model error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
